WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.210
- [Interviewer] Okay, Raul.

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.770
- Yeah.
- Raul, where you from?

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.603
Where were you born?

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.030
- [Raul] Chihuahua, Mexico.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:06.863
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your family.

00:00:06.863 --> 00:00:08.260
You had both parents growing up?

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.150
- [Raul] No, my mother is in Mexico

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.240
and my father is citizen here in U.S.A.,

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.410
but he died, let's say five years ago.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.413
I meeted him three times.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.826
I was raised with my mom only.

00:00:23.826 --> 00:00:24.918
- [Interviewer] Oh, so your
dad wasn't really in your life?

00:00:24.918 --> 00:00:27.677
- No, only three times in my life.

00:00:27.677 --> 00:00:29.410
- [Interviewer] And
how was your childhood?

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.243
- How what?

00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:31.420
- [Interviewer] How was your childhood?

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.835
- Ah, I'm the man in the family, you know?

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.670
I have to grow up fast

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:41.790
and start help my mom
with money by working.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.220
So I'm start selling, I'm
like paperboy, you know?

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.990
Fourteen years, I start working.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:47.823
- [Interviewer] That's great.

00:00:47.823 --> 00:00:49.890
- So I can help my mom with money

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.010
for school and my sisters.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.245
So we can have some money.

00:00:53.245 --> 00:00:56.980
- [Interviewer] And you
went to school in Mexico?

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.250
- Yeah.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.140
- [Interviewer] How did you learn English?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.127
- Here. (chuckles)

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.113
- [Interviewer] You came here what age?

00:01:03.113 --> 00:01:06.907
- I come here when I 24
years old to start working.

00:01:06.907 --> 00:01:08.490
- [Interviewer] And how old are you now?

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.343
- I'm 42.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:14.040
And I'm start learning with
a TV with a closed caption,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.620
and with my friends.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.060
So I wanna work here, so I
say, "I need to learn English."

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.010
And I never feel afraid to speak it,

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.070
so I say, "Yeah, if somebody
laughs me, I will learn!"

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:26.903
- [Interviewer] That's the key!

00:01:26.903 --> 00:01:29.160
- Yeah, and my friends is show me,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.361
like, "Eh, don't say this word,

00:01:30.361 --> 00:01:32.660
you have to say it this way."

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:33.620
That's how I learn.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.453
- [Interviewer] That's how you learn.

00:01:34.453 --> 00:01:35.286
- Yeah.

00:01:35.286 --> 00:01:37.890
- [Interviewer] And at 24, you
did what when you came here?

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.723
You were working?

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:39.880
- Yeah.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.870
I come in first, I have
a competition with,

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.130
I used to work with Motorola,

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.817
so they have the
competition here in U.S.A.

00:01:46.817 --> 00:01:50.670
And I liked, when I have a chance,

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.963
they closed the fabric,

00:01:56.168 --> 00:01:57.230
and they paid me my money,

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.787
so I just come back here and say,

00:01:58.787 --> 00:02:01.937
"Oh, I'm going to try to find
some job here and stay here,"

00:02:01.937 --> 00:02:04.413
and yeah, I stay here,
working construction,

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.471
tried to find anything, you know?

00:02:07.471 --> 00:02:09.410
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
and you like it here?

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.320
- Yeah, I like it, yeah.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.070
- [Interviewer] How does it
compare to your life in Mexico?

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.272
- Oh, here is better.

00:02:14.272 --> 00:02:16.960
When I start working here, I can help my,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.960
I have another brothers, so
I help them get his study.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.851
One is engineer, another is nursing?

00:02:25.851 --> 00:02:27.557
So I help -
- An engineer?

00:02:27.557 --> 00:02:29.950
- Yeah, so I help my brothers
to pay his school over there.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:30.783
- [Interviewer] They're in Mexico still.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:31.870
- Yeah.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.060
- [Interviewer] And are
you a legal citizen?

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:34.893
- No.

00:02:34.893 --> 00:02:35.726
- [Interviewer] You're not?

00:02:35.726 --> 00:02:36.559
- No, I never can get nothing

00:02:36.559 --> 00:02:38.910
because my dad never put that paper.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.360
He never helped me to
get my status here legal.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.810
- [Interviewer] And so
today you're living where?

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.010
You're on Skid Row?

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.703
- No, I just, I have a hotel room.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.090
Yeah, the key program?

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:53.980
I'm staying there.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.780
- [Interviewer] Okay, and are
drugs a part of your life?

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.370
- Not really, sometimes, yeah.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.931
Because it's like,

00:03:01.931 --> 00:03:05.847
I need to get off too
much problems in my -

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.839
All these problems,
sometimes I stress too much,

00:03:09.839 --> 00:03:13.210
they press me, yeah, take
me down to use drugs,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.735
trying to forget a little bit.

00:03:15.735 --> 00:03:17.500
All the problems I have -

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.740
I open one, my company,

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:22.640
my painting business company four times.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.220
And every time it's going down.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.620
Everything, I lose everything.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.240
- [Interviewer] And why is that?

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.363
- Because I always have to trust somebody.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.340
And put all the money in the bank account

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:38.170
for IRAs, for pay insurance,
worker's comp, disability.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.920
And they can take the money, you know?

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.900
And I no have access

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.733
because I no have a

00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:43.969
social security number.
- Yeah, you're just -

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:44.802
- You know?

00:03:44.802 --> 00:03:45.635
- [Interviewer] You're just winging it.

00:03:45.635 --> 00:03:47.650
- Yeah, I only have that debit card,

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.300
I can take 300 bucks and that's it.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.292
I can't sign a check, nothing.

00:03:51.292 --> 00:03:55.883
They always have 100%
control of the money.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.928
So every time is,
somebody's using the money,

00:03:59.928 --> 00:04:02.100
they start steal the money because I make,

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:07.100
I can make 30,000 in one project,
20, 24, 12, 8000, 10,000.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.658
They pay me big contracts, you know?

00:04:12.658 --> 00:04:13.640
- [Interviewer] And
they're paying you cash?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.010
- No, check.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.340
- [Interviewer] And you
don't, do you pay taxes?

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.173
- Yeah.

00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:18.006
- [Interviewer] You do?

00:04:18.006 --> 00:04:20.710
- Yeah, I have, the other way
I have to have the company,

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.740
legal company, with all the
insurance and pay taxes,

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:24.573
you know?

00:04:24.573 --> 00:04:26.290
- [Interviewer] And
being an illegal alien,

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.830
how does that work?

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.930
- I have to use somebody.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.190
He helped to put the company

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.090
and I have to trust all the money him,

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.100
he need to make

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:36.933
all the payments.
- Oh, that's when

00:04:36.933 --> 00:04:37.766
you get burned.

00:04:37.766 --> 00:04:39.680
- Yeah, and that is always burned me.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.130
Because the people, they
no wanna do it right.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.179
So they say, "No, I'm going to pay cash."

00:04:44.179 --> 00:04:46.440
And they start using
cash, cash, cash, cash.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.273
They block me.

00:04:47.273 --> 00:04:48.460
I have to (sighs).

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:49.570
They left me with nothing.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.070
I say, "Well, nothing I can do

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.200
no more."
- So what's the solution?

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.520
- I used to say, I say,

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.010
"I have enough, I don't want no problem,"

00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:01.240
and I'm thinking, try to find
a way, but it's hard for me.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.670
Because I don't have that social
security number, you know?

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.320
So I can put the company only in my name.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.193
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.003
- I travel, I go to Florida,

00:05:10.003 --> 00:05:14.460
to different states to paint.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.906
Because I get a contract.

00:05:15.906 --> 00:05:19.670
I work with really, really good companies.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.170
- [Interviewer] So it's
great that you're working

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.710
and willing to work and
able to get good work, but -

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.326
- The problem, yeah -
- You got a problem.

00:05:25.326 --> 00:05:27.550
- Is how can trust people.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.383
I always trust,

00:05:28.383 --> 00:05:31.570
but I always get lost
because that, the money.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.640
- [Interviewer] Do you have children

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.670
or a wife or girlfriend?

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:37.170
- No, mm-mm, no.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.080
When I have a girlfriend

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.460
is the same problem, so. (laughs)

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.670
I say, "No, no, no more mix."

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:42.650
- [Interviewer] That's
another conversation.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.950
- Yeah, because it's the
same thing, you know?

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.830
One time I have a girlfriend,
she no work, nothing.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:52.710
I give you 2500 each week.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.010
On, man, she get all upset

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.550
because I spent 20 bucks one time.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:58.710
Because I helped out my friend

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.500
to get a membership in the
gym and I paid 20 bucks.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.678
Oh, she called me, like,
"Ey, why you spend 20 bucks?"

00:06:03.678 --> 00:06:04.910
Come on!
- You'd been giving her

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:05.743
how much?

00:06:05.743 --> 00:06:06.576
- Yeah!

00:06:06.576 --> 00:06:07.409
- [Interviewer] How much did you give her?

00:06:07.409 --> 00:06:09.890
- 2500 each week.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:10.723
- [Interviewer] 2500 a week?

00:06:10.723 --> 00:06:14.310
- Yeah, and she start
screaming for 20 bucks.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.868
Oh, man, I said, "I no
want this." (chuckles)

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:19.840
This is a problem I don't
want no more in my life.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:21.490
- [Interviewer] So you prefer, you still,

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:23.630
with these obstacles, with these problems,

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:25.760
you'd rather live here?
- Yeah, it's always, yeah,

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.397
so now I just move here and say,

00:06:29.397 --> 00:06:33.072
"I need start settle down
and check what I can do."

00:06:33.072 --> 00:06:36.225
I need to find somebody I
can trust, really trust.

00:06:36.225 --> 00:06:37.804
- [Interviewer] No kidding.

00:06:37.804 --> 00:06:38.700
- Because I -
- And if you were

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.018
to go back to Mexico, what would you do?

00:06:41.018 --> 00:06:41.993
- I can work.

00:06:41.993 --> 00:06:42.920
- [Interviewer] You can work?

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.743
- Yeah, I can find any, yeah.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.160
The same thing I can do
here, I can do over there.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:52.340
Over there I can, I know
how to work machines,

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:56.240
like CNC router, like tools.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.323
- [Interviewer] And what
stops you from doing that?

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.573
- The pay over there,

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.510
it's not really good.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:03.520
- [Interviewer] You make very little?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.120
- I can make more money here,

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.450
and I wanna build my house over there

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:12.450
or make my things here, the
life here, I lose my truck.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.713
I buy that, a Silverado, 2011.

00:07:17.473 --> 00:07:22.473
I paid cash in one year,
11,000 in one year.

00:07:22.559 --> 00:07:24.470
- [Interviewer] So now
you have no vehicle?

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.777
- Yeah, and I have to lose it

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:28.450
because that is a problem, you know?

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:30.870
When I lose money for other things,

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.617
I have to start selling my tools.

00:07:32.617 --> 00:07:35.123
Because I need to pay
the people, my workers.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.910
I can't leave with money my workers.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.370
- [Interviewer] So you had
no problems with the law,

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.203
anything like that?

00:07:41.203 --> 00:07:42.036
- No.

00:07:42.036 --> 00:07:42.869
- [Interviewer] Nothing like that.

00:07:42.869 --> 00:07:43.702
- Mm-mm.

00:07:43.702 --> 00:07:46.160
- [Interviewer] You're
just trying to make a buck?

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:47.770
- Yeah.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:50.130
And I always lose, all a lot of money,

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.603
all my machines, everything.

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:53.719
They are expensive machines,

00:07:53.719 --> 00:07:56.910
and every time, every
time is the same thing.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.680
- [Interviewer] As a man born in Mexico,

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.350
is everyone born in Mexico

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.339
trying to figure out a
way to come to the U.S.?

00:08:04.339 --> 00:08:05.172
- Not really.

00:08:05.172 --> 00:08:06.005
- [Interviewer] Not really?

00:08:06.005 --> 00:08:07.810
- My first time I wanna come here

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:09.987
is because my dad, I wanna say,

00:08:09.987 --> 00:08:14.487
"Help me to get a study
here, or let me get a job."

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:16.810
And he never helped me,

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.919
so I say, "Well, I will do it myself."

00:08:18.919 --> 00:08:20.260
- [Interviewer] What was your dad's story?

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.093
Why was he not in your life?

00:08:21.093 --> 00:08:23.800
- Oh, he just moved here,

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.203
he say, "I no have kids,"
and he forget about us.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.710
He make money for himself.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.480
He get married, he have another -

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.270
I have a half brother I never meet.

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:37.924
He never told me, I find out for myself.

00:08:37.924 --> 00:08:38.770
- [Interviewer] I mean,
your solution might be

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:41.210
marrying a nice girl here in America.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.043
- Yeah, but -

00:08:42.043 --> 00:08:43.288
- [Interviewer] Who you can trust?

00:08:43.288 --> 00:08:45.363
- I no wanna marry somebody

00:08:45.363 --> 00:08:46.920
just to get the paper because

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.870
that's not me.
- No, no, no,

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:48.736
I'm not saying -

00:08:48.736 --> 00:08:49.569
- People, they -
- I'm not saying

00:08:49.569 --> 00:08:50.402
that kind of relationship.

00:08:50.402 --> 00:08:52.390
- Yeah, people, they do
that, and I no like that.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.223
- [Interviewer] Yeah, no, no, I -

00:08:53.223 --> 00:08:55.298
- If I wanted to marry somebody I loved -

00:08:55.298 --> 00:08:56.305
- [Interviewer] No, that's the only way.

00:08:56.305 --> 00:08:57.247
- Yeah, yeah!
- That's the only way.

00:08:57.247 --> 00:08:59.645
- Because people, they get twisted,

00:08:59.645 --> 00:09:01.121
I no give me money, no, uh-uh,

00:09:01.121 --> 00:09:02.451
I no want that kind of problems.

00:09:02.451 --> 00:09:03.780
- [Interviewer] I'm not
suggesting anything other

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.520
than falling in love and
marrying somebody you trust.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.660
- Because it's too many
problems, you do that.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:11.480
And for me, that's out of the question.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.073
I never going to get married somebody

00:09:13.073 --> 00:09:14.518
just for the papers.

00:09:14.518 --> 00:09:15.790
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.851
- That is something wrong for me.

00:09:17.851 --> 00:09:19.200
- [Interviewer] Do people
do that quite often?

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.033
- Yeah.

00:09:20.033 --> 00:09:20.866
- [Interviewer] They do?

00:09:20.866 --> 00:09:24.503
- Yeah, I try to find
somebody, no, uh-huh, no no.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:28.130
I don't want that kind
of problems in my life.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.370
- [Interviewer] How did you
come to the United States?

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:30.760
How did you get here?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:31.917
Is it difficult?

00:09:31.917 --> 00:09:33.560
- No, I had a visa.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:34.630
- [Interviewer] But
it's harder now, right?

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:35.777
- Yeah.

00:09:35.777 --> 00:09:38.610
Love where I am, I just keep
working, trying to do it.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:39.820
- [Interviewer] So if your brothers wanted

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:41.600
to come to the U.S.,
they couldn't do it now?

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.013
- Mm-mm, I don't think so, no, mm-mm.

